---
title: "The Travelling Salesman problem"
format: html
image: 'tsp_game_map.png'
categories: [Combinatorics, Algorithms, Discrete maths, Optimisation]
---


Between the Circadian Rhythm stop and this one, the trail passes six other stops -- ≤, √, ≥, σ, ≠ and φ. Suppose you wanted to visit each of the stops once whilst minimising the distance that you travel.

This is the **Travelling Salesman Problem** (TSP) -- one of the most famous problems in mathematics and computer science. It sounds simple: just try every order of stops and keep the shortest. With 5 stops there are only 12 distinct routes to check. With 10 stops there are already 181,440. With 20 stops there are over 60 quadrillion -- so many that a computer checking a billion routes every single second would still need about two years to get through them all. Trying every option, which works fine for a handful of stops, becomes hopeless almost immediately -- and no computer, however fast, escapes that by brute force alone.


Real versions of this problem sit behind delivery route planning, circuit board drilling, and DNA sequencing. 

::: {.content-hidden when-format="pdf"}


The app below shows eight of the trail stops: **Ω Circadian Rhythm** (fixed as your start) and **μ Travelling Salesman** (fixed as your end), plus six stops in between -- ≤, √, ≥, σ, ≠ and φ. Tap those six, in whichever order you think gives the shortest route from start to end, then use the toggle in the sidebar to compare:

- **Your route** -- the order you tapped the six middle stops in.
- **Optimal route** -- the true shortest order, found by checking all 720 possibilities exactly.

With six stops to order there are 720 possible routes in total -- still few enough for a computer to check every single one in an instant, which is exactly what the app does for the optimal route. Switch between the two and see how close your guess got.


::: {#fig-tsp .content-hidden when-format="pdf"}
```{=html}
<style>
  #tsp-app, #tsp-app * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  #tsp-app {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    max-width: 1040px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  #tsp-app .tsp-canvas-wrap {
    flex: 1 1 620px;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  #tsp-app .tsp-sidebar {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  #tsp-app h5 {
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  #tsp-app #tsp-status {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  #tsp-app button#tsp-clear {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    cursor: pointer;
